":\"event\"},{\"inputs\":[],\"name\":\"MIN_PRICE_IMPACT_BPS\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"uint256\",\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"uint256\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"},{\"inputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"bytes\",\"name\":\"strategyCalldata\",\"type\":\"bytes\"},{\"internalType\":\"uint256\",\"name\":\"flashloanAmount\",\"type\":\"uint256\"}],\"name\":\"execute\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"uint256\",\"name\":\"netOutput\",\"type\":\"uint256\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"nonpayable\",\"type\":\"function\"},{\"inputs\":[],\"name\":\"orchestrator\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"address\",\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"address\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"details\":\"Calldata layout (ABI-encoded):           bytes32  user_tx_hash               \\u2014 hash of the user tx being backrun (for audit)           address  pool                       \\u2014 DEX pool where price impact occurred           address  token_in                   \\u2014 token to sell into impact (restores price)           address  token_out                  \\u2014 token received           uint256  amount_in                  \\u2014 amount to swap           uint256  min_profit                 \\u2014 minimum net profit required           uint256  max_slippage_bps            \\u2014 maximum allowed slippage (e.g. 50 = 0.5%)           uint256  estimated_price_impact_bps  \\u2014 off-chain-computed price impact estimate         Flow: flashloan(token_in) -> backrun swap (captures price impact)               -> swap back -> repay flashloan -> profit to OrchestratorIMPORTANT TRUST-BOUNDARY NOTE (not a bug fix, a design fact you should know):         `estimated_price_impact_bps` is a value supplied by the caller (your orchestrator),         not something this contract independently verifies against live pool reserves.         The check below is a floor on a *claim*, not a guarantee about *reality* \\u2014 it protects         you only to the extent you trust whatever computed that number off-chain. If you want         an on-chain guarantee instead of a trust-based one, this contract would need to read         pool reserves/price directly and compute impact itself, which is a real design decision         (which oracle/pool-reading method to standardize on) that has to be made deliberately,         not defaulted silently inside a \\\"bug fix.\\\" Flagging it rather than quietly changing         the security model out from under you.\",\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"execute(bytes,uint256)\":{\"params\":{\"flashloanAmount\":\"Amount of token_in received from flashloan provider.\",\"strategyCalldata\":\"ABI-encoded params (see layout above).\"},\"returns\":{\"netOutput\":\"       token_in amount returned (flashloanAmount + profit).\"}}},\"title\":\"MevOfa \\u2014 v13 Final\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"execute(bytes,uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Execute a MEV backrun.\"}},\"notice\":\"Phase 4: MEV-OFA (Order Flow Agreement) backrunning strategy.         Backruns user transactions included in the same bundle.         OFA compliance enforced off-chain by the L4 Security layer.         Builder blacklist enforced at the relay/bundle-submission layer \\u2014 NOT on-chain.         Called via call() from OmegaOrchestrator (NOT delegatecall).\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/strategies/MevOfa.sol\":\"MevOfa\"},\"evmVersion\":\"cancun\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[\":@openzeppelin/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\":ds-test/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/lib/forge-std/lib/ds-test/src/\",\":erc4626-tests/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/lib/erc4626-tests/\",\":forge-std/=lib/forge-std/src/\",\":openzeppelin-contracts/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\":openzeppelin/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/\"],\"viaIR\":true},\"sources\":{\"lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC